"explanation": "To neutralize an acidic food, a basic (alkaline) substance is required. According to the pH scale, values below 7 are acidic, 7 is neutral, and values above 7 are basic. Baking soda has a pH of 8-9, making it the only basic substance among the options. Citrus fruit (pH 2-3) is highly acidic, while dairy (pH 5-7) and water (pH 6-7) are acidic to neutral. Therefore, baking soda is the most effective neutralizer.",
